// Title: Hiding User Account Via SpecialAccounts Registry Key
// Sigma ID: f8aebc67-a56d-4ec9-9fbe-7b0e8b7b4efd
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems), frack113
// Date: 2022-07-12 | Modified: 2023-01-26
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1564.002
// Description: Detects modifications to the registry key "HKLM\Software\Microsoft\Windows
//   NT\CurrentVersion\Winlogon\SpecialAccounts\Userlist" where the value is set to "0" in order to
//   hide user account from being listed on the logon screen.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://thedfirreport.com/2022/07/11/select-xmrig-from-sqlserver/
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/40b77d63808dd4f4eafb83949805636735a1fd15/atomics/T1564.002/T1564.002.md#atomic-test-3---create-hidden-user-in-registry
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_special_accounts.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey contains "\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Winlogon\\SpecialAccounts\\UserList" and RegistryValueData =~ "DWORD (0x00000000)"
